<Prose title="Writ next to Obsidian" description="Both keep notes as Markdown files in a folder, and both can open the same one. Obsidian is the deeper tool. Writ asks less of you before the first sentence." path="/vs/obsidian/" lead="Both keep notes as Markdown files in a folder, and both can open the same folder. Obsidian is the deeper tool. Writ asks less of you before the first sentence, and it is the one that is already open.">
  <h2>Side by side</h2>
  <table>
    <tbody>
    <tr><th></th><th>Obsidian</th><th>Writ</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Your files</td><td>Plain .md in a folder you chose.</td><td>Plain .md in a folder you chose. It opens the folder Obsidian wrote, as it is.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>First run</td><td>Choose a folder, then settle the settings.</td><td>Opens on <code>~/Writ</code> and asks nothing. Change the folder later if you want to.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Getting to it</td><td>Launch the app.</td><td>Already running. One hotkey over any app.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Links</td><td><code>[[Wikilinks]]</code>, backlinks, graph.</td><td>The same syntax. Backlinks in the Connections panel with the sentence each sits in; a graph of the open note or the whole folder.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Properties and tags</td><td>Frontmatter and <code>#tags</code>.</td><td>Read from the same frontmatter and the same <code>#tags</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Plugins</td><td>Thousands, installed per folder.</td><td>None. Text transforms, rewriting and an MCP server are built in.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>AI</td><td>Through community plugins.</td><td>An MCP server for the assistant you already use, and a chat pane over the notes you attach. Both off by default.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Mobile and sync</td><td>Apps on every platform, paid sync.</td><td>Desktop only. Sync is whatever you do with the folder.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Rendering</td><td>Live preview and reading view.</td><td>Source beside the rendered note, or either alone. Also HTML, Mermaid and KaTeX.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Price</td><td>Free for personal use; sync and publish are paid.</td><td>Free. MIT.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
  </table>
  <h2>One folder, both apps</h2>
  <p>Point Writ at the folder Obsidian uses and the notes open from where they are. Links, aliases, properties, tags, callouts and embeds read as written. Writ skips <code>.obsidian/</code> and never writes to it, so Obsidian keeps working from the same folder. The <a href={`${base}/guides/obsidian-vault-files/`}>guide</a> lists what carries over and what does not.</p>
  <h2>Where Obsidian is the better tool</h2>
  <p>Canvas, block references, templates, a plugin for anything, your phone in sync. Writ does none of it, and a note a plugin wrote shows the text the file holds.</p>
  <h2>Where Writ is the easier one</h2>
  <p>There is nothing to set up. The window is there on a hotkey, the note is a file from the first keystroke, and you never decide on a structure before writing. When you want a program to read your notes, it is one command from Settings, and you approve each program by hand.</p>
  <div class="ctas">
    <a href={`${base}/download/`} class="btn btn-primary">Download Writ</a>
    <a href={`${base}/`} class="btn btn-text">What Writ does</a>
  </div>
</Prose>
